      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if an attacker intercepts the salt, the protection from brute-forcing precomputed rainbow tables remains strong. Since a unique salt is used for every password, the attacker cannot use a single pre-computed dictionary file to crack many accounts. They would still have to perform a separate, computationally expensive brute-force attack for each individual password hash.",
